Step 1: Install Node.js
Download and install Node.js from:https://nodejs.org/en/download
Run the .msi installer and complete the installation with the default options.

Step 2: Open PowerShell as Administrator
Search for PowerShell → Right Click → Run as Administrator

Step 3: Enable Script Execution
Run:PowerShell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned

When prompted, type:Y
and press Enter.

Step 4: Verify Node.js Installation
Check Node.js version:
PowerShell
node -v

Check npm version:
PowerShell
npm -v

Example:
Plain Text
v22.x.x
10.x.x


Step 5: Install TypeScript Globally
PowerShell
npm install -g typescript

Verify:
PowerShell
tsc -v


Step 6: Create a Project Folder

Navigate to any drive or location where you want your project.

Example:PowerShell
D:
mkdir ProTypeScript
cd ProTypeScript

Current location:
D:\ProTypeScript


Step 7: Initialize npm Project
PowerShell

npm init -y
npm install --save-dev typescript
npx tsc --init

You should now see:
D:\ProTypeScript
│
├── node_modules
├── package.json
├── package-lock.json
└── tsconfig.json

Step 8: Create Your First TypeScript File
Create:app.ts


Step 9: Compile TypeScript
PowerShell
tsc app.ts


Step 10: Run the JavaScript
PowerShell
node app.js
